  "body": "Found in M5's review of #666 (#664).\n\n**Today:** #666 disarms an armed Setups pick (part-axis by Edge or Two points, or lay-on-plane) when its rows aren't drawn in a frame. That sweep runs inside `pages::properties`, so it runs only while the **Properties** tab is drawn (shell.rs:945). If the tab is closed, or hidden behind another tab in its dock leaf, the sweep never runs. The pick stays armed, and viewport clicks keep feeding the hidden setup draft.\n\n**Expected:** the sweep runs once per frame whatever the dock shows. Picks whose rows weren't drawn this frame are disarmed, including when the Properties tab isn't drawn at all.\n\n**Done means:** a headless test arms a pick, closes or hides the Properties tab, and clicks the part; the click no longer feeds the setup draft. Reopening shows the pick disarmed with its items kept.",
